  <div class="prose">
    <p>This file lists <strong>{{ goalieHistory.rows.length }}</strong> confirmed NHL starts from the nights on our <a href="{{ '/nhl/starting-goalies/' | url }}">starting goalie board</a>. The board runs from {{ goalieHistory.boardStart | displayDate }} through {{ goalieHistory.boardEnd | displayDate }}. Rows in the file run from {{ goalieHistory.coverageStart | displayDate }} through {{ goalieHistory.coverageEnd | displayDate }}, which is every confirmed start in that span whose cited source is an NHL.com page or an NHL club page. <a href="{{ '/nhl/starting-goalies/history.csv' | url }}">Download the same rows as CSV</a>.</p>
    <p>A row gets in when the board's status is confirmed and the source URL is on nhl.com or nhle.com, including team sites on an nhl.com subdomain and the league's box-score feed. {{ goalieHistory.confirmedNonPrimary }} confirmed board entries stay out because the source is a reporter's post or another site. {{ goalieHistory.expected }} entries are still marked expected, and {{ goalieHistory.unconfirmed }} are unconfirmed. Those stay on the dated boards. The labels are the ones in <a href="{{ '/articles/how-nhl-starting-goalies-get-confirmed/' | url }}">how a starter gets confirmed</a>.</p>
    <p>November 1 and November 2, 2026 are on the board and have no row here. November 2 is still a set of projections. On November 1, Matt Tomkins is confirmed for the Oilers on the board, and the source is an Associated Press reporter's post on X. The nightly board keeps that confirmation. This file does not, because the download is limited to league and club pages.</p>
  </div>

